# ReaImGui from Lua

> **In Zed.** Tools: `reaper_lua_docs_search|get|verify` (ImGui is in the same corpus).
> Pass `verify` an **absolute** `path`.

**Load `reaper-scripting` and `reaper-lua` first**, whichever is not loaded. This skill is
only what is true of ReaImGui.

The structure of a widget is in the note on the `Begin*` that opens it: `get
ImGui_BeginTable`, `ImGui_BeginCombo`, `ImGui_BeginMenu`… returns the whole sequence. A
signature you did not `get` is a signature you guessed. What follows are the frame rules
that never get looked up.

**Two call forms**, same API:

```lua
reaper.ImGui_Foo(ctx, ...)                          -- needs nothing
```
```lua
package.path = reaper.ImGui_GetBuiltinPath() .. '/?.lua;' .. package.path
local ImGui = require 'imgui' '0.10'                -- version string is required
ImGui.Foo(ctx, ...)
```

Without the `package.path` line: `module 'imgui' not found`. Match the form the user's
file already uses.

- **`CreateContext(label)`** — label required, called **once**, outside the loop. There is
  no `DestroyContext` and no `CurrentContext` (C++ names).
- **`End` follows the return type of `Begin`.** Returns `boolean` → `End*` only inside
  the `if`. Returns nothing (`BeginGroup`, `BeginDisabled`) → `End*` always.
  `BeginDisabled(ctx, cond)` takes the condition as an argument. Popups close with
  `EndPopup`, `BeginItemTooltip` with `EndTooltip` (`EndPopupModal` does not exist). This
  is the opposite of Dear ImGui in C++.
- **Collapsed is not closed.** Only `open` ends the loop:

  ```lua
  local function loop()
    local visible, open = ImGui.Begin(ctx, 'Title', true)
    if visible then
      -- ...
      ImGui.End(ctx)
    end
    if open then reaper.defer(loop) end
  end
  ```
- **Flags depend on the call form.** `reaper.ImGui_Cond_Always()` is a function;
  `ImGui.Cond_Always` is a number (calling it: `attempt to call a number value`). No
  enum-shaped names (`ImGuiWindowFlags.X`).
- **Identical labels collide.** In loops wrap each row in `PushID(ctx, i)` / `PopID`;
  for one-offs use `'Mute##' .. i`. No static check sees this.
- **An input widget hands the new value back; it cannot write into your variable.**
  `local changed, buf = ImGui.InputText(ctx, label, buf)` — Lua strings and numbers are
  immutable, so the C++ "pass a buffer to be filled" habit has no equivalent and there is
  no size argument. Assign the **second** return back to the state the widget shows.
- **`Text(ctx, s)` takes one string** — format first. Examples in module form omit `ctx`:
  never count arguments off an example.

## Checklist before replying

- `package.path` line present if and only if the module form is used;
- `CreateContext` has a label and runs once, outside the loop;
- every `End*` matches its `Begin*`'s return type — conditional or not;
- `open`, not `visible`, drives the `defer`;
- repeated labels are ID-scoped; no `DestroyContext`, no enum-shaped flags, no printf `Text`.
